# The OTF glyf table: one variable-length glyph outline per entry, its byte span given by `loca`. Simple glyphs
# (contours of on/off-curve points) are real and tested. Composite glyphs (`number-of-contours < 0`, a glyph
# built from other glyphs by reference) are deliberately out of scope — `otf-glyph-composite-unsupported` keeps
# the bounding box but not the component records, the same "unsupported, not silently wrong" shape `cmap`'s
# `otf-cmap-format-unsupported` uses for a subtable format it doesn't decode.

form otf-glyph-point
  link x, like number
  link y, like number
  link on-curve, like boolean

form otf-glyph
  case otf-glyph-empty
  case otf-glyph-simple
    link x-min, like number
    link y-min, like number
    link x-max, like number
    link y-max, like number
    link contours
      like list
        like list
          like otf-glyph-point
    link instructions
      like list
        like u8
  case otf-glyph-composite-unsupported
    link x-min, like number
    link y-min, like number
    link x-max, like number
    link y-max, like number
